  "record": {
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "The prone turn used a flat degrees-per-second rotation while the crawl animation was active, which made the character visibly rotate even when little movement occurred. Rotation is now earned from actual horizontal crawl distance: no movement gives no rotation, and each completed amount of crawl movement contributes a proportional turn budget. Hold W and turn the camera slowly and quickly; the visible turn must track actual crawl progress rather than rotating in place.",
